# What must never reach the build context.
#
# Without this the daemon receives the whole working tree on every build -- `.git`, both
# `node_modules` trees, every worktree's `.venv`, and `.cache/corpus`, which is several
# repositories cloned for the test suite. That is slow on every rebuild and it puts things in an
# image that have no business being there.
#
# Two of these matter for more than speed. `.env` and friends are how a local credential ends up
# baked into a distributable image, and `tools/` holds machine-specific shims resolved against
# this host's paths, which would be wrong inside a Linux container and wrong silently.

.git
.github
.gitignore

# Rebuilt inside the image by their own toolchains, and platform-specific if copied.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
web/dist

# Machine-local: shims resolved against this host, and a corpus of cloned repositories.
tools/
.cache/

# Never bake a credential into an image.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Not part of the product.
docs/
.claude/
.superpowers/

# Markdown is deliberately NOT excluded wholesale. A `**/*.md` rule here cost a build: both
# manifests declare a `readme`, and the build backend fails when the file it names is absent, so
# excluding `src/README.md` broke `sync-core` with nothing but "os error 2" to say why. These
# files are bytes; the directories above are what actually take space.
